    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive base-running and high-ceiling matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leads our lineup with an elite 80.98 score, as the combination of a favorable matchup against Flaherty and his dynamic platoon advantage makes him our primary catalyst for stolen bases. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** provides an elite floor at 78.29; despite a slight park penalty, his xwOBA of 0.476 remains the gold standard for our offense against Junk. We are also leaning heavily on **Christian Yelich** (75.76) in the leadoff spot; his ability to exploit Peralta\u2019s slow delivery makes him a high-efficiency play for stolen base upside, crucial for closing our gap in the most scarce category.\n\nWhile we are starting a deep roster, **Chase Meidroth** was our most difficult exclusion, falling short of our efficiency floor with a 32.38 score. His marginal output was effectively killed by the matchup against deGrom, whose elite SP_xERA of 3.02 renders almost any hitter a liability. We also exercised caution with **Junior Caminero** (55.19); although he maintains a respectable score, his battle against the formidable Cease and a poor SP skill adjustment serves as a reminder to prioritize matchup over raw talent. As we navigate the day, keep a close eye on **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** against Sheehan; while their projections are solid, their SP skill rating is slightly suppressed, necessitating a watchful eye on in-game performance to ensure our efficiency holds steady throughout the evening.",
